Sval: keep a user's media keys, gamepads and document Picture-in-Picture
from a tab an agent controls

While an agent controls a tab, Sval's chrome stops the user's input at the
window that shows it, but some input reaches a page without passing there.
Media keys and the system's media controls act on the main controller
MediaControlService picks among the active MediaControllers, gamepad input
reaches every non-background window that listens (GamepadManager), and a
document Picture-in-Picture window takes the user's input for the page that
opened it, in a window of its own. This adds a parent-set BrowsingContext
field, SvalAgentInControl, which Sval's chrome sets on such a tab, and hooks
that hand over to Sval's SvalAgentInControl.cpp: the tab's MediaController
is not active while the field holds, so the keys go to another tab's media;
GamepadManager treats the tab's windows as background ones; and
DocumentPictureInPicture::RequestWindow refuses the tab's pages, whose open
window closes as the field is set.

